From b7c92819048569c061abf3526f951d569ea793ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:35:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 103/104] packetizer: mlp: let a break cost one frame, not the
 rest of the block

The same shape as the a/52 and dca packetizers, which it is a copy of: the
remainder of a block comes back still flagged, the second flush finds the
timestamp spent, and the undated block is released by the "wait for the first
PTS" gate below.

Unmeasured, unlike the other two. The only carriage of this codec I could
generate is truehd in matroska, which hands over one frame per block, so the
remainder is empty and the flag never returns: four second item looped three
times with --input-repeat, 4796 frames and one stamped output per pass either
way. The fix is by analogy with the measured sites and changes nothing on that
content.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/packetizer/mlp.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/packetizer/mlp.c b/modules/packetizer/mlp.c
index 8b1f6532a3..0a86c7048f 100644
--- a/modules/packetizer/mlp.c
+++ b/modules/packetizer/mlp.c
@@ -287,6 +287,16 @@ static block_t *Packetize( decoder_t *p_dec, block_t **pp_block )
                 block_Release( p_block );
                 return NULL;
             }
+
+            /* What is left of this block once a frame has been taken out of
+             * it comes straight back here, and the break belongs to the seam
+             * the block arrived on, not to the rest of the block: leaving the
+             * flag set makes every following frame flush the parser again,
+             * and the second flush arrives with the block's timestamp already
+             * spent, so the remainder is dropped for want of one - and each
+             * flush arms the outbound flag again, stamping another frame the
+             * decoder then acts on. */
+            p_block->i_flags &= ~BLOCK_FLAG_DISCONTINUITY;
         }
 
         if( !date_Get( &p_sys->end_date ) && p_block->i_pts <= VLC_TICK_INVALID )
